\pard\sa80\sl276\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs40\b Liberty Campus Radio Station - GTA III v1.0 ASI Design\b0\par
\pard\sa240\sl276\slmult1\cf7\fs22 Technical Specification & Audio Programming Guide (Eventide III Edition)\par

\pard\sb240\sa100\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs28\b Overview\b0\par
\pard\sa140\sl300\slmult1\cf2\fs20
In vanilla GTA III v1.0, the radio system is hardcoded to 9 playable FM stations (IDs {\f1\cf5 0\u8211?8}: Head Radio through Chatterbox FM), plus User Track ({\f1\cf5 9}), Police Scanner ({\f1\cf5 10}), and Radio Off ({\f1\cf5 11}). Adding a 10th FM station purely via audio files is not supported because {\f1\cf5 cMusicManager} relies on fixed-size track arrays, hardcoded GXT keys ({\f1\cf5 FEA_FM0\u8211?FEA_FM9}), and hardcoded bounds checks throughout {\f1\cf5 gta3.exe}.\par
\pard\sa180\sl300\slmult1\cf2\fs20
In Eventide III, all ASI plugins are compiled directly with MSVC ({\f1\cf5 cl.exe}) against verified GTA III v1.0 memory addresses (no {\f1\cf5 plugin-sdk} dependency). Because {\f1\cf5 EmergencyRadio.asi} already hooks the core {\f1\cf5 cMusicManager} tuning and HUD pipeline, the Liberty Campus community college station ({\b WLSU 88.5}) should be integrated directly into {\f1\cf5 plugins/EmergencyRadio/EmergencyRadio.cpp} using a virtual station ID and Miles Sound System ({\f1\cf5 Mss32.dll}) streaming.\par

\pard\sb240\sa100\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs28\b 1. Adding the Virtual Station in the ASI Plugin\b0\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\cf2\fs20
Rather than hex-patching every fixed array inside {\f1\cf5 cMusicManager}, inject a virtual station slot ({\b ID 13}, {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO}) directly into {\f1\cf5 EmergencyRadio.cpp} and stream the audio via {\f1\cf5 Mss32.dll} (using the same IAT pattern as {\f1\cf5 PauseMusic.cpp}):\par

\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Safe Virtual Slot ID (ID 13):} {\cf2 In GTA III v1.0, ID {\f1\cf5 9} is {\f1\cf5 USERTRACK} (MP3 Player), {\f1\cf5 10} is {\f1\cf5 POLICE_RADIO}, {\f1\cf5 11} is {\f1\cf5 RADIO_OFF} / {\f1\cf5 STREAMED_SOUND_CITY_AMBIENT}, and {\f1\cf5 12} is {\f1\cf5 STREAMED_SOUND_WATER_AMBIENT}. Using {\b ID 13} prevents any collision with user MP3s or ambient track enums.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Integrate into EmergencyRadio Hooks:} {\cf2 GTA III v1.0 does not have a {\f1\cf5 cMusicManager::ChangeRadioChannel} function; station cycling is driven by {\f1\cf5 ADDR_NUM_RETUNE_PRESSES} ({\f1\cf5 0x650B80}) inside {\f1\cf5 cMusicManager::GetNextCarTuning} ({\f1\cf5 0x57E5A0}), {\f1\cf5 Hook_ServiceGameMode} ({\f1\cf5 0x57D690}), and {\f1\cf5 AdvanceRadioStation}. Insert {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO (13)} after Chatterbox FM ({\f1\cf5 8}) whenever Staunton collision is loaded (and update the mouse-wheel {\f1\cf5 stationCount} calculation accordingly). This automatically supports in-car, on-foot, emergency vehicles, and scroll-wheel tuning.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Mute Native Radio & Stream via Miles (Mss32.dll):} {\cf2 While {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO} is active, suppress native {\f1\cf5 cSampleManager::SetStreamedVolume} output (set native volume to {\f1\cf5 0}) and open {\f1\cf5 audio/WLSU.mp3} (plus a looped {\f1\cf5 audio/WLSU_static.wav} bed) using {\f1\cf5 ADDR_DIG_DRIVER} ({\f1\cf5 0x8F1A24}) and {\f1\cf5 _AIL_open_stream} / {\f1\cf5 _AIL_set_stream_volume}. Sync stream position to a live wall-clock/modulo offset on start so it behaves like a continuous live broadcast, scale volume by {\f1\cf5 cSampleManager::m_nMusicVolume} ({\f1\cf5 0x7341E1}, {\f1\cf5 0..127}), pause on {\f1\cf5 CTimer::m_UserPause} ({\f1\cf5 0x95CD7C}) / {\f1\cf5 CTimer::m_CodePause} ({\f1\cf5 0x95CDB1}), and close handles inside a {\f1\cf5 cSampleManager::Terminate} ({\f1\cf5 0x57A28C}) hook.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Draw the Station HUD Name:} {\cf2 In {\f1\cf5 Hook_DisplayRadioStationName} ({\f1\cf5 0x57E6D0}), map {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO} to {\f1\cf5 L"WLSU 88.5 - Liberty Campus"} and render it via {\f1\cf5 CFont} using the native cyan radio banner colors ({\f1\cf5 \{147, 196, 211\}} tuned, {\f1\cf5 \{102, 133, 143\}} while retuning) and {\f1\cf5 ADDR_DISPLAY_TIMER} ({\f1\cf5 0x650BA1}).}\par

\pard\sb240\sa100\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs28\b 2. Gating by Staunton Island Collision & Transmitter Range\b0\par
\pard\sa120\sl300\slmult1\cf2\fs20
GTA III v1.0 tracks the currently loaded island collision in {\f1\cf5 CCollision::ms_collisionInMemory} ({\f1\cf5 0x941514}, {\f1\cf5 int32_t}) alongside {\f1\cf5 CGame::currLevel} ({\f1\cf5 0x8F6250}, {\f1\cf5 int32_t}): {\f1\cf5 1 = LEVEL_INDUSTRIAL} (Portland), {\f1\cf5 2 = LEVEL_COMMERCIAL} (Staunton Island), and {\f1\cf5 3 = LEVEL_SUBURBAN} (Shoreside Vale).\par

\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Hard Dial Cutoff (Off-Island):} {\cf2 Check {\f1\cf5 *reinterpret_cast<const int32_t*>(0x941514) == 2} ({\f1\cf5 ms_collisionInMemory == LEVEL_COMMERCIAL}). Whenever Portland or Shoreside collision is active, omit {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO} from {\f1\cf5 AdvanceRadioStation}. If the player is already tuned to WLSU while crossing Callahan Bridge or the Porter Tunnel, let distance attenuation carry the broadcast into full static first, then auto-advance off the station once collision switches away from Staunton.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Campus-Centered Range Falloff (On-Island):} {\cf2 Real college radio stations operate low-power transmitters (10\u8211?100 watts). Center the 2D transmitter coordinates on {\b Liberty Campus ({\f1\cf5 UNIVERS})} at {\b X = 180.0, Y = -240.0} (verified against {\f1\cf5 GTA3.ZON}, where {\f1\cf5 UNIVERS} spans {\f1\cf5 X [117.27..239.27]}, {\f1\cf5 Y [-411.62..-61.62]}). Because {\f1\cf5 Mss32.dll} lacks built-in real-time low-pass/mono DSP filters, simulate signal degradation by crossfading {\f1\cf5 WLSU.mp3} down while fading the looped {\f1\cf5 WLSU_static.wav} bed up based on 2D distance from {\f1\cf5 (180.0, -240.0)}.}\par

