\pard\sb240\sa100\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs28\b 3. Station Identity & Programming Concept\b0\par
\pard\sb120\sa80\sl276\slmult1\cf2\fs24\b Broadcast Configuration\b0\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Callsign & Dial Frequency:} {\cf2 WLSU (Liberty State University) (placed in the 88.1\u8211?91.9 MHz reserved non-commercial/educational FM band; billed on air as 88.5 FM).}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Target Demographics:} {\cf2 Campus residents, Staunton indie scene, and late-night commuters.}\par

\pard\sb120\sa80\sl276\slmult1\cf2\fs24\b Programming Vibe\b0\par
\pard\sa140\sl300\slmult1\cf2\fs20 Freeform college-radio format spanning late-90s indie/emo, space-rock, 2-Tone ska, punk, roots dub, and goth post-punk, paired with deadpan, under-caffeinated student DJ bumpers between tracks.\par

\pard\sb120\sa80\sl276\slmult1\cf2\fs24\b Freeform Rotation & Sequencing Arcs\b0\par
\pard\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf2\fs20 Rotation consists of distinct mini-arcs separated by 5\u8211?10 second deadpan student DJ bumpers:\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Arc 1 (90s Indie / Space-Rock):} {\cf2 First Day Back \u8211? "Gone On" \u8594? Hum \u8211? "Diffuse"}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Arc 2 (2-Tone Ska / Punk):} {\cf2 The Specials \u8594? The Beat \u8211? "Mirror in the Bathroom"}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa120\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Arc 3 (Late-Night Dub / Goth Post-Punk):} {\cf2 Augustus Pablo \u8594? Bauhaus \u8211? "Bela Lugosi's Dead"}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b Featured Artists:} {\cf2 Hum, Built to Spill, Pinback, Sunny Day Real Estate, Unwound.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b DJ Persona:} {\cf2 Uninterested, monotone student volunteers making minimal effort on graveyard shifts, featuring deadpan station IDs and passive-aggressive campus event announcements.}\par

\pard\sb160\sa80\sl276\slmult1\cf6\fs20\b Sample Student DJ Bumper Scripts\b0\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b The Unattended Art Opening:} {\cf2 "You're listening to WLSU, Liberty State University. Quick reminder that the Fine Arts Department is hosting their 'Found Objects and Urban Decay' gallery tonight in the Student Union basement until 11. There are free saltines and lukewarm tap water. Nobody showed up to the last one, so Derek from Sculpture is threatening to drop out if at least four people don't sign the guestbook."}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b The Campus Parking / Construction Complaint:} {\cf2 "That was Hum. If you're parked in Lot C near Fort Staunton, Campus Security would like to remind you that towing starts at midnight to make room for the new Panlantic construction staging area. Apparently, paying forty grand a year in tuition doesn't cover asphalt. Anyway, here's The Specials."}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b The Obligatory Club Plug:} {\cf2 "88.5, WLSU. The Liberty Campus Philosophy Club is meeting tomorrow at noon by the Belleville Park fountain to debate whether any of us actually have free will. Spoiler: if you're listening to college radio at two in the morning, you don't."}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b The Equipment / Pledge Drive Guilt Trip:} {\cf2 "You're locked into WLSU, broadcasting at a blistering fifty watts from northern Staunton. If the signal starts cutting out before you even hit Newport, blame the Athletics Department\u8212?they took our transmitter upgrade budget for new turf. Don't call the request line; the phone's been unplugged since October."}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa180\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b The Dorm Noise / Midnight Breakfast PSA:} {\cf2 "Before we get into Augustus Pablo, Housing wants me to announce 'Midnight Pancakes' in the freshman commons. Please note that 'midnight' is a suggestion, the syrup is rationed, and whoever keeps pulling the fire alarm in Rockford Hall at three in the morning is the reason we're all miserable."}\par

\pard\sb240\sa100\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs28\b 4. Implementation Blueprint (Eventide III)\b0\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b 1. Audio Assets:} {\cf2 Package one continuous broadcast mix ({\f1\cf5 audio/WLSU.mp3}) and a short seamless FM static loop ({\f1\cf5 audio/WLSU_static.wav}) into {\f1\cf5 modloader/Eventide/audio/} (and {\f1\cf5 scripts/build.ts} packaging).}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b 2. Virtual Station & Dial Gating:} {\cf2 In {\f1\cf5 EmergencyRadio.cpp}, define {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO = 13} and {\f1\cf5 ADDR_COLLISION_IN_MEMORY = 0x941514}. Update {\f1\cf5 AdvanceRadioStation} to include {\f1\cf5 WLSU_RADIO} only when {\f1\cf5 ms_collisionInMemory == 2}. If active off-island, auto-step to the next valid station and stop the WLSU streams.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b 3. Dual-Stream Miles Playback:} {\cf2 Reuse the {\f1\cf5 Mss32.dll} IAT pointers from {\f1\cf5 PauseMusic.cpp} ({\f1\cf5 ADDR_DIG_DRIVER = 0x8F1A24}, {\f1\cf5 _AIL_open_stream}, {\f1\cf5 _AIL_set_stream_volume}, {\f1\cf5 _AIL_pause_stream}, {\f1\cf5 _AIL_set_stream_ms_position}, and {\f1\cf5 cSampleManager::Terminate} hook at {\f1\cf5 0x57A28C}) to manage {\f1\cf5 g_wlsuStream} and {\f1\cf5 g_wlsuStaticStream}.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa100\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b 4. Signal Falloff & Native Mute:} {\cf2 Each tick in {\f1\cf5 Hook_ServiceAmbience} / {\f1\cf5 Hook_ServiceGameMode}, compute 2D distance from player ped/vehicle to {\f1\cf5 (180.0f, -240.0f)}, calculate program/static weights per the matrix, apply {\f1\cf5 cSampleManager::m_nMusicVolume} ({\f1\cf5 0x7341E1}), and pass {\f1\cf5 0} to native {\f1\cf5 setStreamedVol} while WLSU is playing.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa120\sl300\slmult1\cf4\fs20 {\f2\bullet}\tab{\b 5. HUD & Build:} {\cf2 Add {\f1\cf5 targetStation == WLSU_RADIO} in {\f1\cf5 Hook_DisplayRadioStationName} and build via {\f1\cf5 deno task build --only=emergencyradio}.}\par
